 the semi-final (4:05.07). In the final " [:a {:href "/athletes/73712"} "Berny Boxem-Lenferink"] " (NED) led the first lap, but Bragina then took over, and increased the pace dramatically. She had a 10-metre gap at the bell and held it throughout the final circuit, finishing in a world record 4:01.38. The first five finishers also broke Bragina’s world record from the semi-final and in all there were 12 marks ahead of the pre-München world record."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "335"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77168"} "Lyudmila Bragina"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "4:06.47 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "4:05.07 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "4:01.38 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "132"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69673"} "Gunhild Hoffmeister"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "4:12.80 (2 h4)"] [:td {} "4:07.94 (3 h1)"] [:td {} "4:02.83 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "218"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/71798"} "Paola Cacchi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "4:09.53 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "4:07.83 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "4:02.85 